xref:specialize_routineTypeDef[$specialize_routineTypeDef(routineTypeDefIR, typeIR'^{asterisk}^)]

. If let ``routineTypeIR`` be ``routineTypeDefIR``:
 .. Check that ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ( ``routineTypeIR``, ``·`` ).
. Else:
 .. Let ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` be ``tid^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that the length of ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` is equal to the length of ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^``.

   .... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ typeIR' )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
   .... Return ( ``xref:subst_routineType[$subst_routineType(theta, routineTypeIR)]``, ``·`` ).
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that the length of ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0`` and the length of ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^`` is equal to ``0``.

   .... Let ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:fresh_tids[$fresh_tids(the length of tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^)]``.
   .... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ +TID+ tid~fresh~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
   .... Return ``( xref:subst_routineType[$subst_routineType(theta, routineTypeIR)], tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ )``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that the length of ``tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0`` and the length of ``tid^{asterisk}^`` is equal to the length of ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^`` and the length of ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0``.

   .... Let ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:fresh_tids[$fresh_tids(the length of tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^)]``.
   .... Let ``typeIR~arg_new~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeIR'^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``( +TID+ tid~fresh~ )^{asterisk}^``.
   .... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ typeIR~arg_new~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
   .... Return ``( xref:subst_routineType[$subst_routineType(theta, routineTypeIR)], tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ )``.

xref:specialize_constructorTypeDef[$specialize_constructorTypeDef(constructorTypeIR +<+tid^{asterisk}^ +,+ tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^+>+, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)]

. Let ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` be ``tid^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` is equal to the length of ``typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ typeIR~arg~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
  ... Let ``constructorTypeIR~subst~`` be ``xref:subst_constructorType[$subst_constructorType(theta, constructorTypeIR)]``.
  ... Return ( ``constructorTypeIR~subst~``, ``·`` ).
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0`` and the length of ``typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^`` is equal to ``0``.

  ... Let ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:fresh_tids[$fresh_tids(the length of tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ +TID+ tid~fresh~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
  ... Let ``constructorTypeIR~subst~`` be ``xref:subst_constructorType[$subst_constructorType(theta, constructorTypeIR)]``.
  ... Return ( ``constructorTypeIR~subst~``, ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` ).
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0`` and the length of ``tid^{asterisk}^`` is equal to the length of ``typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^`` and the length of ``typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0``.

  ... Let ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:fresh_tids[$fresh_tids(the length of tid~hidden~^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Let ``typeIR~arg_new~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``( +TID+ tid~fresh~ )^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Let ``theta`` be ``+{+( tid~tparam~ +:+ typeIR~arg_new~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
  ... Let ``constructorTypeIR~subst~`` be ``xref:subst_constructorType[$subst_constructorType(theta, constructorTypeIR)]``.
  ... Return ( ``constructorTypeIR~subst~``, ``tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` ).

xref:canon[$canon(typeIR'')]

. If let ``namedTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``polyTypeDefIR +<+typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``namedTypeIR``.

 .. Let ``typeIR`` be ``xref:specialize_typeDef[$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)]``.
