. Return ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR'[$is_defaultable_typeIR'($canon(typeIR))]``.

xref:is_defaultable_typeIR'[$is_defaultable_typeIR'(typeIR'')]

. If let ``primitiveTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``: return ``true``.
 .. Else if ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+ERROR+``: return ``true``.
 .. Else: return ``true``.
. Else if let ``numberTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``true``.
. Else if let ``aliasTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``aliasTypeIR``.

 .. Return ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``.
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``, for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``typeIR +[+++_+++]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ ++_++ +{+( typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``, for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ ++_++ +{+( typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``, for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ ++_++ +{+( typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``, for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.
 return ``true``.
. Else:
 .. If let ``+ENUM+ ++_++ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``enumTypeIR``: return ``true``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)]``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``false``.

xref:is_equalable_typeIR[$is_equalable_typeIR(typeIR)]

