xref:bin_eq[$bin_eq(value, value')]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``primitiveValue~a~`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``primitiveValue~b~`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``primitiveValue~a~`` is equal to ``primitiveValue~b~``.
  ... Else if let ``number`` be ``value``:
   .... If let ``+D+ i~a~`` be ``number``:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``number'`` be ``value'``.

    ..... Let!~type~ ``+D+ i~b~`` be ``number'``.

    ..... Return ``i~a~`` is equal to ``i~b~``.
   .... Else if let ``w~a~ +W+ i~a~`` be ``number``:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``number'`` be ``value'``.

    ..... Let!~type~ ``w~b~ +W+ i~b~`` be ``number'``.

    ..... Return ``w~a~`` is equal to ``w~b~`` and ``i~a~`` is equal to ``i~b~``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``number'`` be ``value'``.

    ..... Let!~type~ ``w~b~ +S+ i~b~`` be ``number'``.

    ..... Return ``w~a~`` is equal to ``w~b~`` and ``i~a~`` is equal to ``i~b~``.
  ... Else if let ``+[+value~a~^{asterisk}^+]+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+[+value~b~^{asterisk}^+]+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``xref:bin_eqs[$bin_eqs(value~a~^{asterisk}^, value~b~^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+(+value~a~^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+(+value~b~^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``xref:bin_eqs[$bin_eqs(value~a~^{asterisk}^, value~b~^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+[+value~a~^{asterisk}^ +#+ +(+++_++ +;+ n~s_a~+)++]+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+[+value~b~^{asterisk}^ +#+ +(+++_++ +;+ n~s_b~+)++]+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``xref:bin_eqs[$bin_eqs(value~a~^{asterisk}^, value~b~^{asterisk}^)]`` and ``n~s_a~`` is equal to ``n~s_b~``.
  ... Else if let ``+STRUCT+ tid~a~ +{+( value~f_a~ id~f_a~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+STRUCT+ tid~b~ +{+( value~f_b~ id~f_b~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``tid~a~`` is equal to ``tid~b~`` and ``xref:bin_eqs_fields[$bin_eqs_fields(( value~f_a~, id~f_a~ )^{asterisk}^, ( value~f_b~, id~f_b~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+HEADER+ tid~a~ +{+( value~f_a~ id~f_a~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+HEADER+ tid~b~ +{+( value~f_b~ id~f_b~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``tid~a~`` is equal to ``tid~b~`` and ``xref:bin_eqs_fields[$bin_eqs_fields(( value~f_a~, id~f_a~ )^{asterisk}^, ( value~f_b~, id~f_b~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ tid~a~ +{+( value~f_a~ id~f_a~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``+HEADER_UNION+ tid~b~ +{+( value~f_b~ id~f_b~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value'``.

   .... Return ``tid~a~`` is equal to ``tid~b~`` and ``xref:bin_eqs_fields[$bin_eqs_fields(( value~f_a~, id~f_a~ )^{asterisk}^, ( value~f_b~, id~f_b~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Else if let ``enumValue`` be ``value``:
   .... If let ``tid~a~ +.+ id~f_a~`` be ``enumValue``:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``enumValue'`` be ``value'``.

    ..... Let!~type~ ``tid~b~ +.+ id~f_b~`` be ``enumValue'``.

    ..... Return ``tid~a~`` is equal to ``tid~b~`` and ``id~f_a~`` is equal to ``id~f_b~``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``enumValue'`` be ``value'``.

    ..... Let!~type~ ``tid~b~ +.+ id~f_b~ +#+ value~f_b~`` be ``enumValue'``.

    ..... Return ``tid~a~`` is equal to ``tid~b~`` and ``id~f_a~`` is equal to ``id~f_b~`` and ``xref:bin_eq[$bin_eq(value~f_a~, value~f_b~)]``.
  ... Else if let ``invalidHeaderValue`` be ``value``:
   .... Check that ``invalidHeaderValue`` matches pattern ``+{#}+``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``invalidHeaderValue'`` be ``value'``.

   .... Check that ``invalidHeaderValue'`` matches pattern ``+{#}+``.
 return ``true``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``numberValue`` be ``value``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``w~a~ +V+ i~a~ +#+ ++_++`` be ``numberValue``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``numberValue'`` be ``value'``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``w~b~ +V+ i~b~ +#+ ++_++`` be ``numberValue'``.

  ... Return ``w~a~`` is equal to ``w~b~`` and ``i~a~`` is equal to ``i~b~``.

xref:bin_eqs[$bin_eqs(value^{asterisk}^, value'^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``value^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. If ``value'^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``: return ``true``.
 .. Else: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. If ``value'^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``: return ``false``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:bin_eq[$bin_eq(++_++, value~b_h~)]`` and ``xref:bin_eqs[$bin_eqs(++_++^{asterisk}^, value~b_t~^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:bin_eqs_fields[$bin_eqs_fields((value, id)^{asterisk}^, (value, id)'^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``(value, id)^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. If ``(value, id)'^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``: return ``true``.
 .. Else: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Check that ``(value, id)'^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.
 return ``false``.
 .. Let ``( value~a_h~, id~a_h~ ) {two-colons} ( value~a_t~, id~a_t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``(value, id)^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``( value~b_h~, id~b_h~ ) {two-colons} ( value~b_t~, id~b_t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``(value, id)'^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Return ``id~a_h~`` is equal to ``id~b_h~`` and ``xref:bin_eq[$bin_eq(value~a_h~, value~b_h~)]`` and ``xref:bin_eqs_fields[$bin_eqs_fields(( value~a_t~, id~a_t~ )^{asterisk}^, ( value~b_t~, id~b_t~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:bin_ne[$bin_ne(value~l~, value~r~)]

. Return ``~xref:bin_eq[$bin_eq(value~l~, value~r~)]``.

