  ... Return ``w +S+ i'''``.
 .. Else if let ``w~r~ +S+ i~r~`` be ``number'``:
  ... Let ``i~l'~`` be ``xref:to_int[$to_int(w~l~, i~l~)]``.
  ... Let ``i~l''~`` be ``xref:shl[$shl(i~l'~, w~r~)]``.
  ... Let ``i~l'''~`` be ``i~l''~`` + ``i~r~``.
  ... Let ``w`` be ``w~l~`` + ``w~r~``.
  ... Let ``i'''`` be ``xref:to_bitstr[$to_bitstr(w, i~l'''~)]``.
  ... Return ``w +S+ i'''``.

xref:bin_land[$bin_land(value, value')]

. Let!~type~ ``primitiveValue`` be ``value``.

. Let!~type~ ``+B+ b~l~`` be ``primitiveValue``.

. Let!~type~ ``primitiveValue'`` be ``value'``.

. Let!~type~ ``+B+ b~r~`` be ``primitiveValue'``.

. Return ``+B+ b~l~ /\ b~r~``.

xref:bin_lor[$bin_lor(value, value')]

. Let!~type~ ``primitiveValue`` be ``value``.

. Let!~type~ ``+B+ b~l~`` be ``primitiveValue``.

. Let!~type~ ``primitiveValue'`` be ``value'``.

. Let!~type~ ``+B+ b~r~`` be ``primitiveValue'``.

. Return ``+B+ b~l~ \/ b~r~``.

xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, value'')]

. If let ``primitiveValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+B+ b`` be ``primitiveValue``.

 .. Return ``xref:cast_bool[$cast_bool(typeIR, b)]``.
. Else if let ``number`` be ``value''``:
 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``number``:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_arbint[$cast_arbint(typeIR, i)]``.
 .. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``number``:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_fixbit[$cast_fixbit(typeIR, w, i)]``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_fixint[$cast_fixint(typeIR, w, i)]``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ tid +{+( value~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value''``:
 .. Return ``xref:cast_struct[$cast_struct(typeIR, tid, ( value~f~, id~f~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ tid +{+( value~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``value''``:
 .. Return ``xref:cast_header[$cast_header(typeIR, tid, ( value~f~, id~f~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else if let ``enumValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``++_++ +.+ ++_++ +#+ value`` be ``enumValue``.

 .. Return ``xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, value)]``.
. Else if let ``sequenceValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Return ``xref:cast_sequence[$cast_sequence(typeIR, value^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else if let ``recordValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+RECORD+ +{+( value id +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordValue``.

 .. Return ``xref:cast_record[$cast_record(typeIR, ( value, id )^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else if let ``defaultValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. Check that ``defaultValue`` matches pattern ``+DEFAULT+``.

 .. Return ``xref:default[$default(typeIR)]``.
. Else if let ``setValue`` be ``value''``:
 .. If let ``+SET+ +{+value+}+`` be ``setValue``:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_set_singleton[$cast_set_singleton(typeIR, value)]``.
 .. Else if let ``+SET+ +{+value~b~ +&&&+ value~m~+}+`` be ``setValue``:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_set_mask[$cast_set_mask(typeIR, value~b~, value~m~)]``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_set_range[$cast_set_range(typeIR, value~l~, value~u~)]``.

xref:default[$default(typeIR)]

. Return ``xref:default'[$default'($canon(typeIR))]``.

xref:default'[$default'(typeIR'')]

. If let ``primitiveTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``:
  ... Return ``+B+ false``.
 .. Else if ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+ERROR+``:
  ... Return ``+ERROR+ +.+ "NoError"``.
 .. Else if ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+STRING+``:
  ... Let ``text~empty~`` be ``""``.
  ... Return ``+"+ text~empty~ +"+``.
. Else if let ``numberTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If ``numberTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+INT+``:
  ... Return ``+D+ 0``.
 .. Else if let ``+BIT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``numberTypeIR``:
  ... Return ``w +W+ 0``.
 .. Else if let ``+INT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``numberTypeIR``:
  ... Return ``w +S+ 0``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``w +V+ 0 +#+ 0``.
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+[+xref:default[$default(typeIR)]^{asterisk}^+]+``.
. Else if let ``typeIR +[+n~s~+]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let ``value^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:repeat_[$repeat_<value>($default(typeIR), n~s~)]``.
 .. Return ``+[+value^{asterisk}^ +#+ +(+0 +;+ n~s~+)++]+``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ tid +{+( typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+STRUCT+ tid +{+( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ tid +{+( typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+HEADER+ tid +{+( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ tid +{+( typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+HEADER_UNION+ tid +{+( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``enumTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If let ``+ENUM+ tid +{+id^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``enumTypeIR``:
  ... Let!~type~ ``id~f_h~ {two-colons} ++_++^{asterisk}^`` be ``id^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ``tid +.+ id~f_h~``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``value~zero~`` be ``xref:cast_arbint[$cast_arbint(typeIR, 0)]``.
  ... Let ``id^?^`` be ``xref:assoc_[$assoc_<value, id>(value~zero~, ( value~f~, id~f~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let!~type~ ``id~zero~`` be ``id^?^``.

    ..... Return ``tid +.+ id~zero~ +#+ value~zero~``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:assoc_[$assoc_<value, id>(value~zero~, ( value~f~, id~f~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.

    ..... Let ``id~zero~`` be ``"__UNSPECIFIED"``.
    ..... Return ``tid +.+ id~zero~ +#+ value~zero~``.

xref:cast_bool[$cast_bool(typeIR, b)]

. Return ``xref:cast_bool'[$cast_bool'($canon(typeIR), b)]``.

xref:cast_bool'[$cast_bool'(typeIR'', b')]

. If let ``primitiveTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``primitiveTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Return ``+B+ b'``.
. Else if let ``numberTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+BIT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``numberTypeIR``.

 .. If ``b'`` is equal to ``true``:
  ... Return ``w +W+ 1``.
 .. Else if ``b'`` is equal to ``false``:
  ... Return ``w +W+ 0``.
. Else if let ``aliasTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``aliasTypeIR``.

 .. Return ``xref:cast_bool[$cast_bool(typeIR, b')]``.

