  ... Return ``·``.

xref:find_matching[$find_matching<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg''~^{asterisk}^, id~r'~ +(+pid~r''~^{asterisk}^+)+, V)]

. Check that ``~xref:check_routine_name[$check_routine_name(id~r~, id~r'~)]``.

. Return ``·``.
. Let ``id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~`` be ``pid~r''~``, for all ``pid~r''~`` in ``pid~r''~^{asterisk}^``, ``bool~param'~`` in ``bool~param'~^{asterisk}^``, and ``id~param'~`` in ``id~param'~^{asterisk}^``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``xref:check_routine_name[$check_routine_name(id~r~, id~r'~)]``.

  ... Check that ``xref:check_arity_more[$check_arity_more(id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~param'~^{asterisk}^)]``.

  ... Return ``·``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``id~arg''~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0``.

  ... Check that ``xref:check_routine_name[$check_routine_name(id~r~, id~r'~)]``.

  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``xref:check_arity[$check_arity(id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~param'~^{asterisk}^)]``.

    ..... Return ``xref:find_match_named[$find_match_named<V>(id~r'~ +(+( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^+)+, V, id~arg''~^{asterisk}^, ( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``xref:check_arity_less[$check_arity_less(id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~param'~^{asterisk}^)]``.

    ..... Return ``xref:find_match_named_default[$find_match_named_default<V>(id~r'~ +(+( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^+)+, V, id~arg''~^{asterisk}^, ( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``id~arg''~^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

  ... Check that ``xref:check_routine_name[$check_routine_name(id~r~, id~r'~)]``.

  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``xref:check_arity[$check_arity(id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~param'~^{asterisk}^)]``.

    ..... Return ( ``id~r'~ +(+( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^+)+``, ``V``, ``·`` ).
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``xref:check_arity_less[$check_arity_less(id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~param'~^{asterisk}^)]``.

    ..... Return ``xref:find_match_unnamed_default[$find_match_unnamed_default<V>(id~r'~ +(+( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^+)+, V, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, ( id~param'~ +#+ bool~param'~ )^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid''^{asterisk}^, V''^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``rid''^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``V''^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``V~h~ {two-colons} V~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``V''^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Check that ``xref:find_matching[$find_matching<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid~h~, V~h~)]`` is equal to ``·``.

 .. Return ``xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid~t~^{asterisk}^, V~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Let ``( rid, V, id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_matching[$find_matching<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid~h~, V~h~)]``.
 .. Return ``( rid, V, id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) {two-colons} xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid~t~^{asterisk}^, V~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<V>(+{+( rid +:+ V )^{asterisk}^+}+, id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``0``.

  ... Let ``id^?^`` be ``id~arg~^?^``, for all ``id^?^`` in ``id^?^^{asterisk}^`` and ``id~arg~^?^`` in ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Check that ``id^?^`` is defined, for all ``id^?^`` in ``id^?^^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``id~arg'~`` be ``id^?^``, for all ``id^?^`` in ``id^?^^{asterisk}^`` and ``id~arg'~`` in ``id~arg'~^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Check that ``xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid^{asterisk}^, V^{asterisk}^)]`` is equal to ``·``.

  ... Return ``·``.
  ... Let ``(rid, V, id*)^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, id~arg'~^{asterisk}^, rid^{asterisk}^, V^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``( rid', V', id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`` be ``(rid, V, id*)^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ( ``rid'``, ``V'``, ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` ).
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``id~arg~^?^`` is equal to ``·``, for all ``id~arg~^?^`` in ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Check that ``xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, ·, rid^{asterisk}^, V^{asterisk}^)]`` is equal to ``·``.

  ... Return ``·``.
  ... Let ``(rid, V, id*)^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:find_matchings[$find_matchings<V>(id~r~, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^, ·, rid^{asterisk}^, V^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``( rid', V', id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`` be ``(rid, V, id*)^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ( ``rid'``, ``V'``, ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` ).

xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<V>(+{+( rid +:+ V )^{asterisk}^+}+, id)]

. Let ``V''^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:find_non_overloaded'[$find_non_overloaded'<V>(+{+( rid +:+ V )^{asterisk}^+}+, id)]``.
. Let!~type~ ``V'`` be ``V''^{asterisk}^``.

. Return ``V'``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``·``.

xref:find_non_overloaded'[$find_non_overloaded'<V>(set<pair<rid, V>>', id)]

. Check that ``set<pair<rid, V>>'`` is equal to ``+{+·+}+``.

. Return ``·``.
. Let ``+{+pair<rid, V>^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``set<pair<rid, V>>'``.
. Let!~type~ ``rid~h~ +:+ V~h~ {two-colons} ( rid~t~ +:+ V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<rid, V>^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``id' +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``rid~h~``.
. If ``id'`` is equal to ``id``:
 .. Let ``V~t_found~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:find_non_overloaded'[$find_non_overloaded'<V>(+{+( rid~t~ +:+ V~t~ )^{asterisk}^+}+, id)]``.
 .. Return ``V~h~ {two-colons} V~t_found~^{asterisk}^``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``V~t_found~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:find_non_overloaded'[$find_non_overloaded'<V>(+{+( rid~t~ +:+ V~t~ )^{asterisk}^+}+, id)]``.
 .. Return ``V~t_found~^{asterisk}^``.

