xref:empty_typingContext[$empty_typingContext]

. Let ``globalTypingLayer`` be +{++CDENV+ ``xref:empty_cdenv[$empty_cdenv]``, +TDENV+ ``xref:empty_tdenv[$empty_tdenv]``, +RDENV+ ``xref:empty_rdenv[$empty_rdenv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``blockTypingLayer`` be +{++ID+ ``""``, +KIND+ ````, +TDENV+ ``xref:empty_tdenv[$empty_tdenv]``, +RDENV+ ``xref:empty_rdenv[$empty_rdenv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``localTypingLayer`` be +{++ID+ ``""``, +KIND+ ````, +TDENV+ ``xref:empty_tdenv[$empty_tdenv]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``TC`` be +{++GLOBAL+ ``globalTypingLayer``, +BLOCK+ ``blockTypingLayer``, +LOCAL+ ``localTypingLayer``+}+.
. Return ``TC``.

xref:bound[$bound(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``+{+·+}+``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Return ``xref:dom_map[$dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+TDENV+)]``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``bound~block~`` be ``xref:bound[$bound(+BLOCK+, TC)]``.
 .. Let ``bound~local~`` be ``xref:dom_map[$dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(TC.+LOCAL+.+TDENV+)]``.
 .. Return ``xref:union_set[$union_set<tid>(bound~block~, bound~local~)]``.

xref:enter[$enter(TC)]

. Return ``TC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame] {two-colons} TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

xref:exit[$exit(TC)]

. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

. Return ``TC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:add_var[$add_var(cursor, TC, id, varTypeIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame))]``.

 .. Let ``++_++ typeIR ++_++ ++_++^?^`` be ``varTypeIR``.
 .. Check that if ``id`` is equal to ``"main"``, then ``xref:is_package_object_typeIR[$is_package_object_typeIR($canon(typeIR))]``.

 .. Let ``frame~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame))]``.

 .. Check that ``id`` is not equal to ``"main"``.

 .. Let ``frame~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<id, varTypeIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``frame'^{asterisk}^`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame'^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame~h~))]``.

 .. Check that ``id`` is not equal to ``"main"``.

 .. Let ``frame~h_update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame~h~, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame~h_update~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_vars[$add_vars(p, TC, id^{asterisk}^, varTypeIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``id^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``varTypeIR^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``TC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``varTypeIR~h~ {two-colons} varTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``varTypeIR^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(p, TC, id~h~, varTypeIR~h~)]``.
 .. Let ``TC''`` be ``xref:add_vars[$add_vars(p, TC', id~t~^{asterisk}^, varTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``TC''``.

xref:add_parameter[$add_parameter(cursor, TC, direction typeIR id value^?^)]

. If ``direction`` matches pattern ````:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``typeIR +CTK+ value^?^``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(cursor, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``direction`` matches pattern ``+IN+``:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``direction typeIR +DYN+ value^?^``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(cursor, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``direction`` matches pattern ``+OUT+``:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``direction typeIR +DYN+ value^?^``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(cursor, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``direction typeIR +DYN+ value^?^``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(cursor, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_parameters[$add_parameters(cursor, TC, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``TC``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_parameter[$add_parameter(cursor, TC, parameterTypeIR~h~)]``.
 .. Let ``TC''`` be ``xref:add_parameters[$add_parameters(cursor, TC', parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``TC''``.

xref:add_constructorParameter[$add_constructorParameter(TC, direction typeIR id value''^?^)]

. If ``value''^?^`` matches pattern ``()``:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``direction typeIR +CTK+ ·``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(+BLOCK+, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``varTypeIR`` be ``direction typeIR +CTK+ value``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_var[$add_var(+BLOCK+, TC, id, varTypeIR)]``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_constructorParameters[$add_constructorParameters(TC, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``TC``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_constructorParameter[$add_constructorParameter(TC, parameterTypeIR~h~)]``.
 .. Let ``TC''`` be ``xref:add_constructorParameters[$add_constructorParameters(TC', parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``TC''``.

xref:add_type[$add_type(cursor, TC, tid, typeDefIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+TDENV+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<tid>(tid, $dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv))]``.

 .. Let ``tdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid, typeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+TDENV+`` set to ``tdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+TDENV+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<tid>(tid, $dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv))]``.

 .. Let ``tdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid, typeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+TDENV+`` set to ``tdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+TDENV+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<tid>(tid, $dom_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv))]``.

 .. Let ``tdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid, typeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+TDENV+`` set to ``tdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_types[$add_types(p, TC, tid^{asterisk}^, typeDefIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``tid^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``typeDefIR^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``TC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``typeDefIR~h~ {two-colons} typeDefIR~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeDefIR^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``xref:add_type[$add_type(p, TC, tid~h~, typeDefIR~h~)]``.
 .. Let ``TC''`` be ``xref:add_types[$add_types(p, TC', tid~t~^{asterisk}^, typeDefIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``TC''``.

xref:add_routine_overload[$add_routine_overload(cursor, TC, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<rid>(rid, $dom_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv))]``.

 .. Let ``rdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+`` set to ``rdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+RDENV+``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<rid>(rid, $dom_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv))]``.

 .. Let ``rdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+RDENV+`` set to ``rdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_routine_non_overload[$add_routine_non_overload(cursor, TC, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+``.
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``rid``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``xref:dom_map[$dom_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv)]``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``rdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+`` set to ``rdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+RDENV+``.
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``rid``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``xref:dom_map[$dom_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv)]``.
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``rdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)]``.
 .. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+RDENV+`` set to ``rdenv~update~``.
 .. Return ``TC'``.

xref:add_constructor[$add_constructor(TC, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)]

. Let ``cdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+CDENV+``.
. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<cid>(cid, $dom_map<cid, constructorTypeDefIR>(cdenv))]``.

. Let ``cdenv~update~`` be ``xref:add_map[$add_map<cid, constructorTypeDefIR>(cdenv, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)]``.
. Let ``TC'`` be ``TC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+CDENV+`` set to ``cdenv~update~``.
. Return ``TC'``.

xref:find_var[$find_var(p', TC, prefixedNameIR)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
  ... Return ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
   .... Return ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``.
   .... Let ``varTypeIR'^?^`` be ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``varTypeIR`` be ``varTypeIR'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``varTypeIR``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_var[$find_var(+GLOBAL+, TC, id)]``.
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
   .... Let ``varTypeIR'^?^`` be ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<id, varTypeIR>(frame^{asterisk}^, id)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``varTypeIR`` be ``varTypeIR'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``varTypeIR``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<id, varTypeIR>(frame^{asterisk}^, id)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_var[$find_var(+BLOCK+, TC, id)]``.

xref:find_value[$find_value(p', TC, prefixedNameIR)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
  ... Let ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ value'^?^`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

  ... Return ``value``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
   .... Let ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ value'^?^`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
   .... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

   .... Return ``value``.
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``.
   .... Let ``varTypeIR^?^`` be ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ value'^?^`` be ``varTypeIR^?^``.

     ...... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``value``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_map[$find_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, id)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_value[$find_value(+GLOBAL+, TC, id)]``.
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
   .... Let ``varTypeIR^?^`` be ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<id, varTypeIR>(frame^{asterisk}^, id)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ value'^?^`` be ``varTypeIR^?^``.

     ...... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``value``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<id, varTypeIR>(frame^{asterisk}^, id)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_value[$find_value(+BLOCK+, TC, id)]``.

xref:find_type[$find_type(p', TC, prefixedNameIR)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ tid`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+TDENV+``.
  ... Return ``xref:find_map[$find_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid)]``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``tid`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+TDENV+``.
   .... Return ``xref:find_map[$find_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid)]``.
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``tid`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``tdenv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+TDENV+``.
   .... Let ``typeDefIR'^?^`` be ``xref:find_map[$find_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``typeDefIR`` be ``typeDefIR'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``typeDefIR``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_map[$find_map<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv, tid)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_type[$find_type(+GLOBAL+, TC, tid)]``.
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``tid`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``tdenv^{asterisk}^`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+TDENV+``.
   .... Let ``typeDefIR'^?^`` be ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv^{asterisk}^, tid)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``typeDefIR`` be ``typeDefIR'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``typeDefIR``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_maps[$find_maps<tid, typeDefIR>(tdenv^{asterisk}^, tid)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_type[$find_type(+BLOCK+, TC, tid)]``.

xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]

. Return ``xref:id_argument[$id_argument(argumentIR)]^{asterisk}^``.

xref:id_argument[$id_argument(argumentIR)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR``.

  ... Return ``·``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``nameIR +=+ ++_++`` be ``argumentIR``:
   .... Return ``nameIR``.
  ... Else if let ``nameIR +=+ +_+`` be ``argumentIR``:
   .... Return ``nameIR``.
  ... Else if ``argumentIR`` matches pattern ``+_+``:
   .... Return ``·``.

xref:find_routine_overloaded[$find_routine_overloaded(cursor, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
  ... Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+``.
  ... Let ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Return ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+``.
  ... Let ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... Return ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

 .. Let ``rdenv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+RDENV+``.
 .. Let ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Let ``(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)^?^`` be ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``( rid, routineTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`` be ``(rid, routineTypeDefIR, id*)^?^``.

   .... Return ( ``rid``, ``routineTypeDefIR``, ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` ).
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.

   .... Return ``xref:find_routine_overloaded[$find_routine_overloaded(+GLOBAL+, TC, id, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

 .. Return ``xref:find_routine_overloaded[$find_routine_overloaded(+BLOCK+, TC, id, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:find_routine_non_overloaded[$find_routine_non_overloaded(p', TC, prefixedNameIR)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Return ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+, id)]``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Return ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(TC.+GLOBAL+.+RDENV+, id)]``.
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``routineTypeDefIR'^?^`` be ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+RDENV+, id)]``.
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let!~type~ ``routineTypeDefIR`` be ``routineTypeDefIR'^?^``.

     ...... Return ``routineTypeDefIR``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<routineTypeDefIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+RDENV+, id)]``.

     ...... Return ``xref:find_routine_non_overloaded[$find_routine_non_overloaded(+GLOBAL+, TC, id)]``.
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Return ``xref:find_routine_non_overloaded[$find_routine_non_overloaded(+BLOCK+, TC, id)]``.

xref:find_constructor_overloaded[$find_constructor_overloaded(TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``cdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+CDENV+``.
 .. Let ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<constructorTypeDefIR>(cdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``cdenv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+CDENV+``.
 .. Let ``id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:ids_arguments[$ids_arguments(argumentIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``xref:find_overloaded[$find_overloaded<constructorTypeDefIR>(cdenv, id, id~arg~^?^^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:find_return_type[$find_return_type(TC)]

. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+FUNCTION+ +->+ typeIR~ret~`` be ``localKind``:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``+ACTION+`` is equal to ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.

  ... Return ``+VOID+``.
. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+EXTERN_METHOD+ +->+ typeIR~ret~`` be ``localKind``:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+`` is equal to ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.

  ... Return ``+VOID+``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``·``.

xref:empty_tableContext[$empty_tableContext]

. Let ``matchPriority`` be +{++VALUES+ ``·``, +INIT+ ``false``, +DELTA+ ``1``, +LARGEST_WINS+ ``true``+}+.
. Let ``matchEntry`` be +{++SIZE+ ``0``, +CONST+ ``true``+}+.
. Return +{++KEYS+ ``·``, +ACTIONS+ ``·``, +PRIORITIES+ ``matchPriority``, +ENTRIES+ ``matchEntry``, +MODE+ ``+NOPRI+``+}+.

xref:add_key[$add_key(TBLC, id, typeIR)]

. Let ``matchKey`` be ( ``typeIR``, ``id`` ).
. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+KEYS+`` set to ``TBLC.+KEYS+ {pp} matchKey``.

xref:add_action[$add_action(TBLC, prefixedNameIR, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, argumentListIR)]

. Let ``matchAction`` be ( ``prefixedNameIR``, ``parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^``, ``argumentListIR`` ).
. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+ACTIONS+`` set to ``TBLC.+ACTIONS+ {pp} matchAction``.

xref:add_table_priority[$add_table_priority(TBLC, n)]

. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+PRIORITIES+.+VALUES+`` set to ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+VALUES+ {pp} n``.

xref:update_mode[$update_mode(TBLC, id, typeIR)]

. Return ``xref:update_mode'[$update_mode'(TBLC, id, $canon(typeIR))]``.

xref:update_mode'[$update_mode'(TBLC, text', typeIR'')]

. If ``text'`` is equal to ``"lpm"``:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... If let ``numberTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
    ..... If let ``+INT+ +<+n+>+`` be ``numberTypeIR``:
     ...... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

     ...... Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+NOPRILPM+ n``.
    ..... Else if let ``+BIT+ +<+n+>+`` be ``numberTypeIR``:
     ...... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

     ...... Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+NOPRILPM+ n``.
    ..... Else:
     ...... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

     ...... Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+NOPRILPM+ n``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let!~type~ ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``aliasTypeIR``.

    ..... Return ``xref:update_mode[$update_mode(TBLC, "lpm", typeIR)]``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+PRI+``.

   .... Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRILPM+``.
. Else if ``text'`` is equal to ``"range"``:
 .. Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRI+``.
 .. Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``+NOPRILPM+ ++_++`` be ``matchMode``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRILPM+``.
. Else if ``text'`` is equal to ``"ternary"``:
 .. Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRI+``.
 .. Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``+NOPRILPM+ ++_++`` be ``matchMode``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRILPM+``.
. Else:
 .. Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NOPRI+``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRI+``.
 .. Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``+NOPRILPM+ ++_++`` be ``matchMode``.

 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRILPM+``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``TBLC``.

xref:find_action[$find_action(TBLC, prefixedNameIR)]

. Return ``xref:find_action'[$find_action'(TBLC.+ACTIONS+, prefixedNameIR)]``.

xref:find_action'[$find_action'(matchAction^{asterisk}^, prefixedNameIR)]

. If ``matchAction^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``( prefixedNameIR', parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, argumentListIR )`` be ``matchAction~h~``.
 .. If ``prefixedNameIR'`` is equal to ``prefixedNameIR``:
  ... Return ( ``parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^``, ``argumentListIR`` ).
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:find_action'[$find_action'(matchAction~t~^{asterisk}^, prefixedNameIR)]``.

xref:find_table_priority_last[$find_table_priority_last(TBLC)]

. Let ``n^{asterisk}^`` be ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+VALUES+``.
. Return ``n^{asterisk}^[the length of n^{asterisk}^ - 1]``.

xref:join_tableEntryState[$join_tableEntryState(tableEntryState, tableEntryState')]

. If ``tableEntryState`` matches pattern ``+NOLPM+``:
 .. If let ``+LPM+ n`` be ``tableEntryState'``:
  ... Return ``+LPM+ n``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``+NOLPM+``.
. Else:
 .. Check that ``tableEntryState'`` matches pattern ``+NOLPM+``.

 .. Return ``+LPM+ n``.

xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix(value)]

. Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value, 0)]``.

xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value, n~prefix'~)]

. Let!~type~ ``number`` be ``value``.

. Let!~type~ ``nat +W+ ++_++`` be ``number``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``nat`` is equal to ``0``.

  ... Return ``n~prefix'~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``n`` be ``++_++``.

  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``nat`` is greater than ``0``.

    ..... Check that ``n`` \ ``2`` is not equal to ``0``.

    ..... Let ``value'`` be ``nat - 1 +W+ n - 1 / 2``.
    ..... Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value', n~prefix'~ + 1)]``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``n~prefix'~`` is equal to ``0``.

    ..... Check that ``nat`` is greater than ``0``.

    ..... Check that ``n`` \ ``2`` is equal to ``0``.

    ..... Let ``value'`` be ``nat - 1 +W+ n / 2``.
    ..... Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value', 0)]``.

xref:Type_wf[Type_wf: ``bound ⊢ typeIR'''``]

. If let ``baseTypeIR`` be ``typeIR'''``:
 .. The relation holds.
. Else if let ``namedTypeIR`` be ``typeIR'''``:
 .. If let ``+TID+ tid`` be ``namedTypeIR``:
  ... Check that ``xref:in_set[$in_set<tid>(tid, bound)]``.

  ... The relation holds.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``typeIR`` be ``xref:specialize_typeDef[$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)]``.
  ... If xref:Type_wf[``bound ⊢ typeIR``] holds:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``aliasTypeIR`` be ``typeIR'''``:
 .. If let ``+TYPEDEF+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``aliasTypeIR``:
  ... Check that ``xref:nestable_typedef[$nestable_typedef(typeIR)]``.

  ... If xref:Type_wf[``bound ⊢ typeIR``] holds:
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else:
  ... Check that ``xref:nestable_new[$nestable_new(typeIR)]``.

  ... If xref:Type_wf[``bound ⊢ typeIR``] holds:
   .... The relation holds.
